# PredGate Champion Baseline CODEOWNERS Setup
#
# GitHub branch protection + CODEOWNERS governs who may merge PRs modifying
# /champion/ or /champion.dvc (no custom CI approval bypass exists).
#
# IMPORTANT: Do NOT commit unconfigured placeholder handles (such as @your-org/...)
# because GitHub's CODEOWNERS linter rejects non-existent users/teams and may
# silently ignore invalid rules. Uncomment ONE of the configurations below and
# replace the handle(s) with real GitHub owners, then enable:
#   Settings -> Branches -> Branch protection rules -> Require review from Code Owners
#
# ── Option A: Personal / User GitHub Account ──────────────────────────────────
# Use individual GitHub usernames (@<username>):
#
# /champion/ @<your-github-username>
# /champion.dvc @<your-github-username>
#
# ── Option B: GitHub Organization Account ─────────────────────────────────────
# Organization teams MUST include the @<org>/ prefix (bare @team-name is parsed
# by GitHub as a personal username, not an org team):
#
# /champion/ @<your-org>/<ml-admins-team> @<your-org>/<ml-reviewers-team>
# /champion.dvc @<your-org>/<ml-admins-team> @<your-org>/<ml-reviewers-team>
